.\\\", which is `defines`, not `specialises`.\"}\n{\"n\": 10, \"grade\": \"wrong-relation\", \"reason\": \"The text merely notes that \\\"The Spectral Action of these theories was later systematically computed... in [ P\\u00e9r19 ]\\\", which is context/fact, not a technique used to obtain the paper's own result.\"}\n{\"n\": 11, \"grade\": \"faithful\", \"reason\": \"The Abstract asserts they are identified: \\\"this allows to state Yang-Mills-Higgs theory... as an explicit random multimatrix model\\\".\"}\n{\"n\": 12, \"grade\": \"wrong-relation\", \"reason\": \"The text contrasts the new framework with almost-commutative manifolds (\\\"in contrast to 'almost-commutative manifolds', the present framework... employs only finite-dimensional algebras\\\"), but does not claim it generalises it.\"}\n{\"n\": 13, \"grade\": \"faithful\", \"reason\": \"Definition 4.1 introduces the term: \\\"If moreover D_{F}=0 above holds, then G_{\\\\text{\\\\char 102\\\\relax}}\\\\times F is called Yang-Mills matrix spectral triple.\\\"\"}\n{\"n\": 14, \"grade\": \"faithful\", \"reason\": \"Proposition 4.6 establishes this formula: \\\"The square of the fluctuated Dirac operator of a Yang-Mills gauge matrix spectral triple that is flat... is given by...\\\"\"}\n{\"n\": 15, \"grade\": \"faithful\", \"reason\": \"Lemma 3.3 establishes the formula: \\\"The square of the Dirac operator of a fuzzy geometry G_{\\\\text{\\\\char 102\\\\relax}}... is D^{2}_{\\\\text{\\\\char 102\\\\relax}} = ...\\\"\"}\n{\"n\": 16, \"grade\": \"faithful\", \"reason\": \"Proposition 5.3 states how the field strength transforms: \\\"\\\\mathscr{F}_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}=[\\\\mathsf{F}_{\\\\mu\\\\nu},\\\\bullet]\\\\mapsto\\\\mathscr{F}_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}^{u}=[\\\\mathsf{F}_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}^{u},\\\\bullet]\\\".\"}\n{\"n\": 17, \"grade\": \"faithful\", \"reason\": \"Definition 4.1 introduces the term: \\\"we say that G_{\\\\text{\\\\char 102\\\\relax}}\\\\times F is a Yang-Mills\\u2013Higgs matrix spectral triple\\\".\"}\n{\"n\":